<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovakia pares 1996 grain crop forecast.</title>
<headline>Slovakia pares 1996 grain crop forecast.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Slovak Statistical Bureau (SUSR) said on Tuesday it had revised downwards its 1996 grain harvest forecast to 2.64-2.71 million tonnes, from a previous estimate of 2.77-2.82 million.</p>
<p>The latest estimate is a result of the third crop survey this year as of August 15.  </p>
<p>SUSR said the latest estimate compared with last year's crop of 2.89 million tonnes.</p>
<p>&quot;As oppposed to the previous estimate, the latest one expects a lower yield, which has effected the whole crop,&quot; the SUSR said in a statement.</p>
<p>Average estimated yield was 3.81 tonnes, from a previous estimate of 3.92 tonnes.</p>
<p>This year's harvest is &quot;considerably&quot; delayed compared with the last year due to rainy whether, the bureau added.</p>
<p>SLOVAK GRAIN CROP ESTIMATES</p>
<p> (thousand tonnes)	    Aug 15 '96    July 15 '96</p>
<p> All grains			 2.64-2.71     2.77-2.82</p>
<p>  Wheat			     1.72-1.77     1.77-1.81</p>
<p>  Barley			     731-755	 793-812</p>
<p>--Bratislava Newsroom +42-7-210-3687</p>
